    {
        "slug": "ei-maternity-leave-job-loss-ruling-ottawa-wont-appeal",
        "title": "Ottawa won't appeal EI ruling for moms laid off on leave",
        "summary": "A court found EI rules discriminate against moms who lose their job around maternity leave. Ottawa now has until September 2027 to fix them.",
        "date": "2026-11-25", "date_label": "November 25, 2026", "read": "4 min read",
        "image": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1758024375456-014f504e88d2?w=1200&h=800&fit=crop&crop=faces&q=80&auto=format",
        "image_alt": "A mother holding her baby while talking on the phone in a kitchen",
        "credit": "Photo via Unsplash",
        "blocks": [
            ("p", "The federal government has confirmed it will not take a major Employment Insurance case to the Supreme Court of Canada. The case was brought by mothers who lost their jobs around the time of their maternity or parental leave and were then denied regular EI benefits. The decision means a Federal Court of Appeal ruling in their favour now stands, and Ottawa has to change the law."),
            ("h", "What the problem was"),
            ("p", "Under the current EI rules, a parent who is laid off shortly before, during or soon after maternity or parental leave can end up with little or no regular EI, the benefit most people rely on after a job loss. The time spent on leave can leave her short of the insurable hours she needs, or she runs into the limit on how many weeks of combined benefits can be paid in one benefit period. In plain terms, taking leave to have a baby could cost a mother the safety net she'd have had if she had never gone on leave."),
            ("p", "According to <a href=\"https://www.canadianlawyermag.com/practice-areas/labour-and-employment/fca-ei-rules-stripping-new-mother-of-job-loss-benefits-discriminate/394633\" rel=\"noopener\">Canadian Lawyer</a>, the rules at issue include the 52-week qualifying and benefit periods, the cap on combined regular and special benefits, and the fact that the qualifying period can be extended for things like illness, but not for time spent on maternity or parental benefits."),
            ("h", "How the case got here"),
            ("p", "The case was started in 2018 by six Quebec women whose job losses happened between 2016 and 2018, with support from the advocacy group Mouvement Action-Chômage de Montréal, <a href=\"https://globalnews.ca/news/12048194/ei-maternity-leave-court-of-appeal/\" rel=\"noopener\">Global News reported</a>. The Social Security Tribunal first ruled for them in 2022. That decision was overturned on appeal within the tribunal in 2024, and the women then took it to the Federal Court of Appeal."),
            ("p", "In early September 2026, a three-judge panel of the Federal Court of Appeal ruled unanimously for the women. The court found the rules violate the equality guarantee in section 15 of the Charter of Rights and Freedoms, because they discriminate on the basis of sex. As the court put it, <a href=\"https://www.narcity.com/court-rules-in-favour-of-new-mothers-denied-ei\" rel=\"noopener\">reported by The Canadian Press</a>, \"only women can become pregnant and give birth.\""),
            ("p", "Justice Gleason, writing for the court, said more generous maternity and parental benefits \"cannot be the forfeiture of regular EI benefits\", <a href=\"https://www.canadianlawyermag.com/practice-areas/labour-and-employment/fca-ei-rules-stripping-new-mother-of-job-loss-benefits-discriminate/394633\" rel=\"noopener\">according to Canadian Lawyer</a>. The court declared the provisions inoperative but suspended that declaration for one year to give the government time to respond. The six women's claims were sent back to the EI Commission to be looked at again."),
            ("h", "What happens now"),
            ("p", "On November 10, the office of federal minister Patty Hajdu, who is responsible for EI, confirmed the government would not appeal, <a href=\"https://www.ctvnews.ca/montreal/article/ottawa-wont-appeal-ei-and-maternity-leave-case/\" rel=\"noopener\">CTV News reported</a>, citing The Canadian Press. The government said it would work on solutions over the coming year. <a href=\"https://www.noovo.info/nouvelles/societe/travail/article/assurance-emploi-et-conge-de-maternite-ottawa-ninterjettera-pas-appel/\" rel=\"noopener\">La Presse Canadienne</a> reported that the deadline to change the law is September 3, 2027."),
            ("p", "As of today, no bill or regulation has been announced, so the EI rules themselves have not changed yet. The case is about the federal Employment Insurance Act, which applies to workers across Canada, including here in B.C. Mouvement Action-Chômage has said thousands of women could benefit; there is no official count."),
            ("p", "If you were laid off around a maternity or parental leave and were refused regular EI, it's worth keeping your paperwork, your Record of Employment and any decision letters. Service Canada, a legal clinic or an employment lawyer can tell you what applies to your own situation."),
            ("think", "I went back to my full-time job after my son was born, and I know how much planning goes into a leave. The idea that losing your job during it could also take away your EI is exactly the kind of motherhood penalty nobody warns you about. Six moms spent eight years fighting this for the rest of us. Now I want to see the fix actually written into the law before the deadline, not at the last minute."),
        ],
        "sources": [
            ("The Canadian Press via Narcity, September 4, 2026", "https://www.narcity.com/court-rules-in-favour-of-new-mothers-denied-ei"),
            ("Global News, September 4, 2026", "https://globalnews.ca/news/12048194/ei-maternity-leave-court-of-appeal/"),
            ("Canadian Lawyer, September 10, 2026", "https://www.canadianlawyermag.com/practice-areas/labour-and-employment/fca-ei-rules-stripping-new-mother-of-job-loss-benefits-discriminate/394633"),
            ("The Canadian Press via CTV News, November 10, 2026", "https://www.ctvnews.ca/montreal/article/ottawa-wont-appeal-ei-and-maternity-leave-case/"),
            ("La Presse Canadienne via Noovo (French), November 10, 2026", "https://www.noovo.info/nouvelles/societe/travail/article/assurance-emploi-et-conge-de-maternite-ottawa-ninterjettera-pas-appel/"),
        ],
    },
    {
        "slug": "baby-brezza-sterilizer-busy-book-recall-canada",
        "title": "Recalled in Canada: Baby Brezza sterilizer and a busy book",
        "summary": "Health Canada recalls a Baby Brezza bottle sterilizer for overheating and a toddler busy book for choking risk, plus a warning on a banned baby walker.",
        "date": "2026-11-25", "date_label": "November 25, 2026", "read": "4 min read",
        "image": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1623707430616-d9f956bcac2b?w=1200&h=800&fit=crop&crop=entropy&q=80&auto=format",
        "image_alt": "Two baby feeding bottles on a table",
        "credit": "Photo via Unsplash",
        "blocks": [
            ("p", "With holiday shopping starting and a lot of baby gear changing hands, here's a round-up of recent Health Canada recalls and warnings that affect babies and toddlers. If you have any of these at home, check the model numbers below."),
            ("h", "Baby Brezza SuperFast Sterilizer Dryer"),
            ("p", "Health Canada has recalled the Baby Brezza SuperFast Sterilizer Dryer, a countertop machine that sterilizes and dries bottles and pump parts. The affected model is BRZ0083 (UPC 886267008313)."),
            ("p", "The problem is overheating. Health Canada says the unit \"can overheat when plugged in and in use\", which creates fire and burn hazards, <a href=\"https://globalnews.ca/news/12140535/baby-brezza-bottle-sterilizer-recall/\" rel=\"noopener\">Global News reported</a>. As of October 29, there had been 20 reports of overheating and melting in Canada and 32 in the U.S. No injuries have been reported."),
            ("p", "About 6,001 units were sold in Canada and 29,000 in the U.S., between September 2023 and November 2026. Health Canada says to stop using it right away. The Quebec-based importer, EI Brand Management Inc., is offering a free replacement through service@elfe.ca or the brand's recall page at babybrezza.ca/en/recalls/brz0083, <a href=\"https://www.cp24.com/news/canada/2026/11/06/thousands-of-items-sold-in-canada-recalled-due-to-fire-and-burn-hazards/\" rel=\"noopener\">CP24 reported</a>."),
            ("p", "The sterilizer was announced alongside other fire and burn recalls in early November, including Bose S1 Pro and S1 Pro+ battery packs for portable speakers and NEWDERY power banks (model ZHX-PB22) sold on Amazon.ca. If you have a portable speaker or a power bank in the diaper bag, those are worth a quick check too."),
            ("h", "Esjay Montessori busy book (blue dinosaur)"),
            ("p", "A toddler activity book sold on Amazon.ca, the blue dinosaur Esjay Montessori busy book, was recalled on October 7 because small red pieces on page 2 can come loose. That's a choking hazard for children under three, <a href=\"https://www.mtlblog.com/amazon-canada-products-recalls\" rel=\"noopener\">MTL Blog reported</a>."),
            ("p", "This one sold widely: 32,340 units in Canada between August 2023 and September 2026. No incidents or injuries had been reported in Canada as of September 22. The fix is simple: unzip and remove the page with the red pieces, write \"RECALLED\" on both sides, throw it out, and email a photo to esjay-service@outlook.com for a free replacement page."),
            ("h", "Warning: MUELODSIC baby walker"),
            ("p", "Health Canada has also warned against a MUELODSIC multifunctional baby walker that was sold on Amazon.ca (Amazon ID B0FWGCCJ14). Baby walkers are banned in Canada because of the risk of falls, including down stairs. Amazon reported 133 units sold in Canada. Because this is a warning and not a recall, there may be no refund. Health Canada's advice is to stop using it and destroy it."),
            ("h", "Recall or warning: what's the difference?"),
            ("p", "A recall means the company is working with Health Canada, so there's usually a refund, repair or replacement. A warning is issued when the seller isn't cooperating, which often happens with products from third-party sellers on online marketplaces. With a warning, you usually can't count on getting your money back, as MTL Blog explained. That's one more reason to check the brand and seller carefully when you buy baby gear online."),
            ("h", "What to do if you have one"),
            ("p", "Stop using the product, check the model or ID number, and follow the steps above. It is illegal to sell or give away a recalled product in Canada, so please don't pass these on through a buy-and-sell group or a hand-me-down bag. You can search every recall and sign up for alerts on the <a href=\"https://recalls-rappels.canada.ca/en\" rel=\"noopener\">Government of Canada recalls site</a>."),
            ("think", "Bottle sterilizers and busy books are on so many baby registries, and a lot of us buy them from Amazon or second-hand without ever checking for recalls. If you're buying gifts for a new baby this season or getting gear from a friend, take two minutes and search the recalls site first. And please share this with the mom group chat. That's how most of us find out."),
        ],
        "sources": [
            ("Global News, November 6, 2026", "https://globalnews.ca/news/12140535/baby-brezza-bottle-sterilizer-recall/"),
            ("CP24, November 5, 2026", "https://www.cp24.com/news/canada/2026/11/06/thousands-of-items-sold-in-canada-recalled-due-to-fire-and-burn-hazards/"),
            ("MTL Blog, November 6, 2026", "https://www.mtlblog.com/amazon-canada-products-recalls"),
            ("Government of Canada: Recalls and safety alerts", "https://recalls-rappels.canada.ca/en"),
        ],
    },
